    "kind": "definition_of_done",
    "summary": "- BOM test.** In `internal/api/api_test.go`, the body literal now uses `\\xef\\xbb\\xbf` instead of `\\\\xef\\\\xbb\\\\xbf`, so the body really starts with a byte order mark. The header still resolves to `name` and `email`, and the test's created-customer assertions pass.\n- Comma-only lines.** `blankRecord` in `internal/api/customers.go` now treats a record as blank only when it is a single empty (or spaces-only) field. A line such as `,,,` is a record with empty fields, so it reports `missing_name`. I updated the `bad` fixture to expect `{\"row\":10,\"error\":\"missing_name\"}` in place of the old blank-ski\n...[truncated]",
